    "content": "## Test Summary\n\nI've completed all 18 tests on the ThreadHive community forum application. Here are the results:\n\n### **PASSED (16 tests):**\n- **FT-1**: User registration, login, logout, and re-login with same credentials ✓\n- **FT-2**: Profile bio and interests editing with persistence ✓\n- **FT-3**: Discussion creation with category, title, and body ✓\n- **FT-4**: Adding replies to discussions with immediate display ✓\n- **FT-5**: Upvote functionality on discussions and replies ✓\n- **FT-6**: Keyword search with proper filtering and empty result feedback ✓\n- **FT-7**: Category filtering with dynamic result updates ✓\n- **FT-8**: Most Active discussions ordered by reply count (descending) ✓\n- **FT-10**: Viewing author's public profile with all details ✓\n- **FT-13**: Session data persistence through logout/login cycle ✓\n- **CS-14**: Missing discussion fields validation with error feedback ✓\n- **CS-17**: Incorrect password rejection during login ✓\n- **CS-22**: Unauthenticated user redirected to login ✓\n- **CT-16**: Trending discussions ordered by upvote count (descending) ✓\n- **CT-19**: Reply count consistency between list and detail views ✓\n- **CT-21**: Community statistics displayed and tracking ✓\n\n### **FAILED (2 tests):**\n- **FT-18**: Session NOT persisted across page reload - user logged out after reload\n- **CT-20**: Trending/Most Active lists lack stated time window in descriptions\n\n### **Key Issues:**\n1. **Session Persistence**: The application doesn't persist authentication across page reloads. Implementing localStorage/sessionStorage for auth tokens would fix this.\n2. **Time Window Documentation**: Trending and Most Active discussions should display what time period they cover (e.g., \"Last 7 Days\", \"Last 30 Days\").\n\nThe forum application is largely functional with solid core features for discussions, profiles, filtering, and voting. The main limitation is the need for improved session management for page reload scenarios."
